IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- s 2(1): the defined terms about BENCHMARKS: financial benchmark, designated benchmark, administering a financial or designated
-- benchmark, providing information in relation to a benchmark, and the corporations authorised, designated or exempted to administer or
-- submit to one. Imports prelude and daydate only.
--
-- How to read a function in this module.
--   Every defined term of s 2(1) is ONE function, named `s 2(1) "<term>" <the thing> is <the term>`, over the facts a person could state.
--   The result is MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--     JUST TRUE   the thing is within the term (a limb of the definition is met and no exclusion applies);
--     JUST FALSE  the TEXT says it is not: a definition that says "means" and no limb is met, or an express exclusion ("but does not include");
--     NOTHING     the text does not say: an "includes" definition (an open list) with no listed limb met.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
--   Every branch that answers "no" carries `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "..."`; every branch that
--   answers "not covered" carries `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`.
--   A limb the Act hands to the Authority, the regulations or another Act ("prescribed", "specified", "as defined in the
--   Banking Act 1970") is an INPUT named for the fact ("the Authority has prescribed ..."), never a thing read from memory.
--   The definitions apply "unless the context otherwise requires" (the chapeau of s 2(1)): that qualification is
--   `s 2(1) the definitions apply unless the context otherwise requires` in sfa-definitions-rest.l4, not repeated here.

§ `s 2(1): benchmarks`

-- src:1680 | “administering a designated benchmark” means —
-- src:1682 | (a) controlling the development of the definition of a
-- src:1683 | designated benchmark for the purpose of determining
-- src:1684 | a designated benchmark;
-- src:1686 | (b) controlling the development of the methodology of
-- src:1687 | determining a designated benchmark;
-- src:1689 | (c) controlling the review of the definition of a
-- src:1690 | designated benchmark for the purpose of
-- src:1691 | determining a designated benchmark;
-- src:1693 | (d) controlling the review of the methodology of
-- src:1694 | determining a designated benchmark;
-- src:1696 | (e) managing any arrangements, processes or
-- src:1697 | mechanisms for the purpose of determining a
-- src:1698 | designated benchmark;
-- src:1700 | (f) collecting, analysing or processing any information
-- src:1701 | or expression of opinion for the purpose of
-- src:1702 | determining a designated benchmark;
-- src:1704 | (g) applying a formula or other methods of calculation to
-- src:1705 | information or expressions of opinion in order to
-- src:1706 | determine a designated benchmark; or
-- src:1708 | (h) monitoring and conducting surveillance of any
-- src:1709 | information or expressions of opinion provided for
-- src:1710 | the purpose of determining a designated benchmark,
-- src:1712 | but does not include providing information in relation to a
-- src:1713 | designated benchmark or any act that is necessary or
-- src:1714 | incidental to providing such information;
@ref s 2(1) "administering a designated benchmark" (src:1680-1714)
GIVEN
    `the act is controlling the development of the definition of a designated benchmark for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act controlling the development of the definition of a designated benchmark for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark?
    `the act is controlling the development of the methodology of determining a designated benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act controlling the development of the methodology of determining a designated benchmark?
    `the act is controlling the review of the definition of a designated benchmark for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act controlling the review of the definition of a designated benchmark for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark?
    `the act is controlling the review of the methodology of determining a designated benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act controlling the review of the methodology of determining a designated benchmark?
    `the act is managing any arrangements, processes or mechanisms for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act managing any arrangements, processes or mechanisms for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark?
    `the act is collecting, analysing or processing any information or expression of opinion for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act collecting, analysing or processing any information or expression of opinion for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark?
    `the act is applying a formula or other methods of calculation to information or expressions of opinion in order to determine a designated benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act applying a formula or other methods of calculation to information or expressions of opinion in order to determine a designated benchmark?
    `the act is monitoring and conducting surveillance of any information or expressions of opinion provided for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act monitoring and conducting surveillance of any information or expressions of opinion provided for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark?
    `the act is providing information in relation to a designated benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act providing information in relation to a designated benchmark (as section 2(1) defines that)?
    `the act is necessary or incidental to providing such information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act necessary or incidental to providing such information?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "administering a designated benchmark" the act is administering a designated benchmark` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act is providing information in relation to a designated benchmark` OR `the act is necessary or incidental to providing such information`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include providing information in relation to a designated benchmark or any act that is necessary or incidental to providing such information"
        IF `the act is controlling the development of the definition of a designated benchmark for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark` OR `the act is controlling the development of the methodology of determining a designated benchmark` OR `the act is controlling the review of the definition of a designated benchmark for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark` OR `the act is controlling the review of the methodology of determining a designated benchmark` OR `the act is managing any arrangements, processes or mechanisms for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark` OR `the act is collecting, analysing or processing any information or expression of opinion for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark` OR `the act is applying a formula or other methods of calculation to information or expressions of opinion in order to determine a designated benchmark` OR `the act is monitoring and conducting surveillance of any information or expressions of opinion provided for the purpose of determining a designated benchmark`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means (a) controlling the development of the definition ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; (d) ...; (e) managing any arrangements, processes or mechanisms ...; (f) collecting, analysing or processing any information ...; (g) applying a formula ...; or (h) monitoring and conducting surveillance ..."

