-- src:2488 | “financial benchmark” means —
-- src:2490 | (a) any price, rate, index or value that is —
-- src:2492 | (i) determined periodically by the application
-- src:2493 | (whether direct or indirect) of a formula or
-- src:2494 | any other method of calculation to information
-- src:2495 | or expressions of opinion concerning
-- src:2496 | transactions in, or the state of, the market in
-- src:2497 | respect of one or more underlying things;
-- src:2499 | (ii) made available to the public (whether free of
-- src:2500 | charge or for payment); and
-- src:2502 | (iii) used for reference —
-- src:2504 | (A) to determine the interest payable or other
-- src:2505 | sums due on deposits or credit facilities;
-- src:2507 | (B) to determine the price or value of any
-- src:2508 | investment product as defined in
-- src:2509 | section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers
-- src:2510 | Act 2001; or
-- src:2512 | (C) to measure the performance of any
-- src:2513 | product offered by a person who is, or
-- src:2514 | who belongs to a class of persons which
-- src:2515 | is, prescribed by regulations made under
-- src:2516 | section 341; or
-- src:2518 | (b) such other price, rate, index or value as may be
-- src:2519 | prescribed by regulations made under section 341 as
-- src:2520 | a financial benchmark,
-- src:2522 | but does not include —
-- src:2524 | (c) a price, rate, index or value determined by, or on
-- src:2525 | behalf of, the Government or a statutory body
-- src:2526 | established under any Act, unless that price, rate,
-- src:2527 | index or value is prescribed as a financial benchmark;
-- src:2529 | (d) a price, rate, index or value determined by a person
-- src:2530 | which is intended to be for the person’s exclusive use
-- src:2531 | in transactions or agreements entered into, or to be
-- src:2536 | entered into, by the person, unless that price, rate,
-- src:2537 | index or value is prescribed as a financial benchmark;
-- src:2539 | (e) the price of a capital markets product; or
-- src:2541 | (f) such other price, rate, index or value as may be
-- src:2542 | prescribed by regulations made under section 341 as
-- src:2543 | not being a financial benchmark;
@ref s 2(1) "financial benchmark" (src:2488-2543)
GIVEN
    `it is determined periodically by applying a formula or other method of calculation to information or expressions of opinion concerning transactions in, or the state of, the market in respect of one or more underlying things` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the price, rate, index or value determined periodically by the application (direct or indirect) of a formula or other method of calculation to information or expressions of opinion concerning transactions in, or the state of, the market in respect of one or more underlying things?
    `it is made available to the public, free of charge or for payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made available to the public (whether free of charge or for payment)?
    `it is used for reference to determine the interest payable or other sums due on deposits or credit facilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used for reference to determine the interest payable or other sums due on deposits or credit facilities?
    `it is used for reference to determine the price or value of an investment product as defined in section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used for reference to determine the price or value of any investment product as defined in section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001?
    `it is used for reference to measure the performance of a product offered by a person, or a class of persons, prescribed by regulations under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it used for reference to measure the performance of any product offered by a person (or a class of persons) prescribed by regulations made under section 341?
    `regulations under section 341 prescribe it as a financial benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations made under section 341 prescribe this price, rate, index or value as a financial benchmark?
    `it is determined by or on behalf of the Government or a statutory body established under an Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the price, rate, index or value determined by, or on behalf of, the Government or a statutory body established under any Act?
    `it is determined by a person and intended for that person's exclusive use in transactions or agreements entered or to be entered into by that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the price, rate, index or value determined by a person and intended for that person's exclusive use in transactions or agreements entered into, or to be entered into, by that person?
    `it is the price of a capital markets product` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the price of a capital markets product?
    `regulations under section 341 prescribe it as not being a financial benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations made under section 341 prescribe this price, rate, index or value as not being a financial benchmark?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "financial benchmark" the price, rate, index or value is a financial benchmark` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`it is determined by or on behalf of the Government or a statutory body established under an Act` AND (NOT `regulations under section 341 prescribe it as a financial benchmark`)) OR (`it is determined by a person and intended for that person's exclusive use in transactions or agreements entered or to be entered into by that person` AND (NOT `regulations under section 341 prescribe it as a financial benchmark`)) OR `it is the price of a capital markets product` OR `regulations under section 341 prescribe it as not being a financial benchmark`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include (c) a price, rate, index or value determined by, or on behalf of, the Government or a statutory body ..., unless that price, rate, index or value is prescribed as a financial benchmark; (d) ... intended to be for the person's exclusive use ..., unless ... prescribed as a financial benchmark; (e) the price of a capital markets product; or (f) such other price, rate, index or value as may be prescribed ... as not being a financial benchmark"
        IF (`it is determined periodically by applying a formula or other method of calculation to information or expressions of opinion concerning transactions in, or the state of, the market in respect of one or more underlying things` AND `it is made available to the public, free of charge or for payment` AND (`it is used for reference to determine the interest payable or other sums due on deposits or credit facilities` OR `it is used for reference to determine the price or value of an investment product as defined in section 2(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001` OR `it is used for reference to measure the performance of a product offered by a person, or a class of persons, prescribed by regulations under section 341`)) OR `regulations under section 341 prescribe it as a financial benchmark`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means (a) any price, rate, index or value that is (i) determined periodically ...; (ii) made available to the public ...; and (iii) used for reference (A) ...; (B) ...; or (C) ...; or (b) such other price, rate, index or value as may be prescribed ... as a financial benchmark"

-- src:2408 | “designated benchmark” means a financial benchmark that is
