    `the Authority has designated it under section 123B to be a designated benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority designated it under section 123B to be a designated benchmark?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "designated benchmark" the benchmark is a designated benchmark` MEANS
    IF `the benchmark is a financial benchmark` AND `the Authority has designated it under section 123B to be a designated benchmark`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a financial benchmark that is designated by the Authority under section 123B to be a designated benchmark"

-- src:2834 | “providing information in relation to a designated benchmark”
-- src:2835 | means providing any information or expression of opinion —
-- src:2837 | (a) to, or for the purpose of passing the information or
-- src:2838 | expression of opinion on to, a person (A)
-- src:2839 | administering a designated benchmark; and
-- src:2841 | (b) that enables A to determine that designated
-- src:2842 | benchmark;
@ref s 2(1) "providing information in relation to a designated benchmark" (src:2834-2842)
GIVEN
    `the information or expression of opinion is provided to, or for the purpose of passing it on to, a person administering a designated benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information or expression of opinion provided to, or for the purpose of passing it on to, a person (A) administering a designated benchmark?
    `it enables that person to determine the benchmark` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it enable that person (A) to determine that benchmark?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "providing information in relation to a designated benchmark" the act is providing information in relation to a designated benchmark` MEANS
    IF `the information or expression of opinion is provided to, or for the purpose of passing it on to, a person administering a designated benchmark` AND `it enables that person to determine the benchmark`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means providing any information or expression of opinion (a) to, or for the purpose of passing the information or expression of opinion on to, a person (A) administering a designated benchmark; and (b) that enables A to determine that designated benchmark"

